qa=['# POP-02A technical and artistic review','','**Technical asset integration: PASS in the tested scope. Streaming readiness: CONDITIONAL / NOT PRODUCTION READY. Artistic acceptance: OPEN; target landscape quality not yet reached.**','','## Validation','','* POP-01 recovered at exact commit `4afbb6f9598a1611df53d0c9f61b6fd1845a3fc7`; bundle and parent ancestry verified.','* Baseline 42/42 tests reproduced. Final suite **58/58 passes**, with all original tests retained. TypeScript/Vite build passes; shared-bundle size warning remains.','* 23 source modules audited; 26 source geometry configurations fingerprinted. Geometry/material/foliage/depth/LOD code is unchanged except the explicit grass batch compatibility patch.','* Real Worker output matches the unchanged synchronous POP generator exactly in an independent browser comparison. Proxy/source modes and density regeneration preserve IDs.','* Unit tests exercise page aggregation/disposal, replacement transforms, partial failure cleanup, stale worker cancellation, shared-resource ownership, orientation, stable fade keys, production seeds, neighboring-page rock suppression and halo bounds.','* Full WebGL run: 34 comparison captures + 10 actual keyboard-driven walking frames + seven end-to-end checks.','* Supplement: matched native multi-draw versus instanced source forest has **0 changed pixels**, mean/max delta 0. All three tree variants and all four grass/rock variants are represented. Six isolated page/backend activation scenarios measured.','* Final default: 128 m instanced pages. Four final camera captures and two real-source re-entry cycles pass. Before/after registrations: %d / %d; renderer counters %s / %s.'%(final['before']['registered'],final['after']['registered'],final['before']['memory'],final['after']['memory']),'* Initial full run: no errors, one PCFSoftShadowMap deprecation/fallback warning. Fixed to explicit supported PCFShadowMap; supplement and final validation have **no errors or warnings**. Earlier captures used that same effective fallback filter.','* No native Android, desktop-GPU FPS, GPU timer-query, VRAM-byte or full heap-retention validation claimed. Stable renderer counters and bounded owner maps are narrower evidence.','','## Final selected profile','','64 m generation chunks; 128 m instanced render pages. Generated descriptors are different from registered source slots and camera/shadow submissions. Grass-rock footprint suppression explains missing grass registrations. Renderer totals include neutral terrain, static canonical water and shadow passes.','','| Camera | Generated | Registered | Pages | Submitted/retained | Calls | Triangles |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|',*rows,'','## Source fidelity and alignment','','Birch direct Mesh versus existing instanced batch: local studio 0 changed pixels; geographic pose 71 / 1,080,000 above delta 12, mean channel delta ~0.0041. Precision/matrix order is the leading explanation, not a proven general large-world precision solution. Intentionally broken opaque depth changes 29,988 pixels. Source alpha-aware shadows are active.','','Grass policy B (terrain orientation) is the selected technical candidate. Policy A (upright with >25% slope rejection) remains selectable. Both keep source geometry. Normal alignment and conservative footprint checks are not a complete triangle-level ground/intersection solver. Source variants remain visibly individual tufts; no new understory, litter, sedge, heath or dune family was invented.','','## Artistic assessment','','* **Promising:** recognizable birch/pine silhouettes, distinct species palettes/materials, source leaf detail and bark, mixed groups, forest openings, real terrain contact and cutout shadows.','* **Below target:** the neutral exposed floor dominates many walking views. Source grass remains too sparse and isolated to read as a rich woodland floor. Adding more objects blindly is not the recommended fix.','* Trunk spacing can still read as relatively even within dense patches. The first forest edge/corridor is inspectable, but enclosure/reveal, understory layers and landmark framing need a separate reviewed composition pass.','* Central Valley stays open and Home Cove thins toward the shore, but neither is artistically finished. Static blue water and neutral ground are deliberately context, not MAT/WTR output.','* The source production stones are cheap angular dressing and can look pale or simple; no premium/hero approval is inferred.','* The local terrain patch and bounded active population have visible outer limits; fog does not make this a full-world panorama. No physical tree/rock collision or approved final hiking path is claimed.','','## Acceptance by requirement','','| Requirement | Result |','|---|---|','| Source geometry/materials and alpha/depth fidelity | Pass in reported reference conditions |','| Deterministic original placement | Pass; POP-01 source protected |','| Original terrain/hydrology preserved | Pass; protected hashes and original tests |','| Real-batch unload/re-entry, stable owner maps | Pass for tested cycles |','| LOD / visibility / transform mapping | Pass in tested settings; source hysteresis resets on page rebuild |','| Actual source-asset screenshots and walking | Pass |','| Streaming performance | Conditional: worker generation works, page activation still stalls and hides dirty pages |','| Artistic quality | Owner review required; premium landscape target not reached |','| Unfinished parallel milestones | Not imported or altered |']
(root/'QA.md').write_text('\n'.join(qa)+'\n')
perf=['# POP-02A measured rendering and activation behavior','','**Software Chromium/SwiftShader only. Not native Android or desktop GPU FPS.**','','The first full run measured six page/backend transitions but its timing arrays retained prior samples. The supplement resets timing arrays per transition; the table below uses those isolated windows. Values are one observed run, not statistical device guarantees. Some setup/GC/compiler scheduling noise remains; do not rank real devices from these numbers.','','| Backend | Page edge | Pages | Registered | Page build samples ms | Max page ms | Sum page ms | Draw calls | Triangles |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for s in supp['performance']:
 perf.append('| %s | %d | %d | %d | %s | %.1f | %.1f | %d | %d |'%(s['backend'],s['pageSize'],s['render']['pages'],s['render']['registered'],' / '.join('%.1f'%n for n in s['pageBuildSamples']),s['maxPageBuildMs'],s['totalPageBuildMs'],s['renderer']['calls'],s['renderer']['triangles']))
perf+=['','**Final provisional choice: instanced 128 m pages.** This had the smallest maximum page-construction observation (~308 ms here) and lower renderer texture counters, trading more draw calls for smaller activation units. Instanced 256 m had a slightly lower aggregate page-build sum but a higher maximum (~612 ms). Native multi-draw reduced draw calls, but did not win page construction in this session. Rendering-page size is not yet hardware-approved.','','This is still far outside an interactive frame budget. The architecture removes chunk generation from the main thread, limits it to one in-flight worker job, coalesces chunk updates and activates at most one render page per frame. It **does not** make a whole source page preemptible. Dirty pages are hidden until replacement, causing temporary disappearance; first allocations, shader compilation, CPU source-batch registration and uploads remain blockers. No average FPS figure is used to hide these spikes.','','Reported worker generation duration is CPU placement work in the Worker. Page build includes source-batch construction, registrations, visibility initialization and buffer staging. CPU `renderer.render` durations include submission and possible upload/driver synchronization; they are not isolated GPU elapsed time. rAF intervals include software rendering and scheduling. Raw samples and maxima are retained in `runtime.json`, `supplement.json` and `final-validation.json`.','','Renderer calls/triangles include terrain, static canonical water, camera and shadow submissions. Multi-draw can internally cull retained shadow geometry in a camera pass, so submission counts differ from the instanced backend even though the matched interior images are pixel-identical. `renderer.info.memory` counts geometry/texture objects, not GPU bytes.','','Real-batch repeated region unload/re-entry is stable for descriptor IDs, registered source counts and renderer counters in both the original 256 m/native run and the final 128 m/instanced run. This does not certify an arbitrary native driver or prove complete JS heap stability. Worker query data/index memory is duplicated versus the render-thread geographic context and requires device profiling.']
(root/'PERFORMANCE.md').write_text('\n'.join(perf)+'\n')
readme='''# POP-02A — nature asset integration review

**Technical integration implemented and tested. Streaming performance conditional; owner art approval open.**

Branch: `feature/pop-02a-nature-asset-integration`, from exact POP-01 `4afbb6f9598a1611df53d0c9f61b6fd1845a3fc7`, whose parent is canonical geography `90d0cb745e8e51a3dc737bd4dc11d6f8c322758b`. Initial integration checkpoint: `2b01a572d7db47654940489abaa77a82ece48245`; final handoff manifest records the final review commit. Local only: no push, merge, publication or deployment.

[Visual review](review.html) · [QA and artistic assessment](QA.md) · [Asset compatibility](ASSET_COMPATIBILITY.md) · [Architecture](ARCHITECTURE.md) · [Performance](PERFORMANCE.md) · [MAT/WTR reconciliation audit](MAT_WTR_COORDINATION.md)

## Delivered

* Original POP-01 recovered and reproduced; its placement code and canonical data remain hash-identical.
* Isolated source library: birch/pine (three variants, source LODs), four source grass variants and four production rocks only (seeds 11,23,37,53). Full provenance and explicit grass batch compatibility patch.
* Real source-family batches driven by POP descriptors, per-page atomic replacement/disposal, shared family ownership, terrain-oriented grass/rocks, conservative rock-footprint suppression and stable ID-based grass fade phases.
* Web Worker near-priority generation with one job in flight and stale-target cancellation. At most one coalesced page activates per frame; page construction still stalls.
* `pop-02a.html` with proxies/source assets, density, seed, page sizes, backends, LOD, grass policies/fade, warm/cool light, shadows, inspection and 17 actual-world cameras.
* 58 passing automated tests; passing TypeScript/Vite build; actual WebGL comparisons, source-fidelity gate, contact sheet, full-resolution captures, actual keyboard walking frames/replay and measured performance limitations.

## Reproduce

```sh
npm ci --no-audit --no-fund
npm test
npm run build
npm run dev
# open /pop-02a.html; /pop-01.html remains intact
CHROME=/path/to/chromium node tools/pop-02a/fidelity.mjs
# The following start/stop their own Vite preview after npm run build:
CHROME=/path/to/chromium node tools/pop-02a/capture.mjs
CHROME=/path/to/chromium node tools/pop-02a/supplement.mjs
CHROME=/path/to/chromium node tools/pop-02a/final-validation.mjs
python3 tools/pop-02a/media.py
python3 tools/pop-02a/review.py
```

`capture.mjs` deliberately switches configurations for comparison. The retained first full series used 256 m / auto pages; `final-*.png` records the selected 128 m / instanced default. The source matrix/depth comparison's geographic pose has 71 small pixel differences; studio comparison and matched full-forest backend comparison are exact. See QA for scope, tolerances and negative control.

`extract.py` is a one-time pinned transitive extraction helper; it refuses an existing destination to protect reviewed compatibility fixes. Normal reproduction uses the already committed source modules, not re-extraction. Imported source whitespace is deliberately retained for byte fidelity; the small compatibility patch includes original blank context lines.

## Remaining gates / POP-02B proposal (not started)

1. **Activation performance first:** keep the unchanged placement engine, but make buffer/page registration resumable or use bounded reusable handle pools with explicit page eviction. Avoid hiding an entire dirty page while retaining full cleanup. Prove max-frame behavior rather than average FPS.
2. Profile canonical-query duplication, JS heap and real GPU resources on desktop and Android. Choose page/backend/density/visibility profiles from device data; do not infer Android readiness from SwiftShader.
3. Review a shared environment-data contract with MAT/GEO/WTR before using material weights as placement authority. Geometric contact and exact water safety must remain independent from blended shading.
4. Artistically review the source trees/grass/production stones, then address forest-floor continuity, patch/edge composition and a short hiking corridor. The bare neutral floor and separated tufts currently miss the premium target. More uniform scattering is not the solution.
5. Resolve source LOD reset transitions, optional near grass shadows and camera/view clearances only through a scoped reviewed follow-up. New shrubs, litter, heath or sedge families require their own approval.

No full-island population, geography edits, MAT/WTR merges, premium rock work, new vegetation families or production terrain streaming was started. Stop after this review package.
'''
(root/'README.md').write_text(readme)
